  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Recovery Assistance in Mykolaiv</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall objective: The creation of an environment conducive for return is enabled through the restoration of critical services, support to key duty-bearers, the creation of dignified livelihood opportunities, and the empowerment of local civil society.
 
Outcome: An improved enabling environment for reintegration and recovery of returnees, IDPs and host community is achieved in Mykolaiv.
 
Output 1: Critical infrastructure is repaired, rehabilitated, and restored in order to create an environment for recovery and reintegration.

Output 2: Job seekers (women and persons of concern (PoCs)) are given support, training, and access to labour opportunities within the reconstruction sector.

Output 3: Duty-bearers&#x2019; capacity to provide essential services as part of the return process has been strengthened.  

Output 4: CSOs have increased capacity and ability to provide services supporting protection, integration and social cohesion at community level</narrative>
  </description>
